From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Set desktop file name for Wayland compositors

Labwc and other wlroots compositors rely on the Wayland app_id matching the
desktop entry basename. KeepSecret installs `org.kde.keepsecret.desktop`, but
the binary name is just `keepsecret`, so Qt can otherwise expose a mismatched
app_id and break icon or launcher association.
---
 src/main.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -53,6 +53,10 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 
     KLocalizedString::setApplicationDomain("keepsecret");
     QCoreApplication::setOrganizationName(u"KDE"_s);
+    // Keep the Wayland app_id aligned with the installed desktop file so
+    // wlroots compositors such as labwc can match launcher metadata, icons,
+    // and window rules correctly.
+    QGuiApplication::setDesktopFileName(u"org.kde.keepsecret"_s);
 
     KAboutData aboutData(
         // The program name used internally.
